Session-lifetime reminder (checkpoint discipline): your session is killed if a turn runs too long (~1 hour), and uncommitted work is lost with it. Commit and push a checkpoint whenever a unit of work is complete, and end the turn with `submit_outcome` + outcome `checkpoint` (tree clean, branch pushed) rather than stretching one turn past the limit. On start, `git log --oneline -5` — continue from your last pushed checkpoint. Use `ready_for_review` only when the full gate is green and the workstream is complete.

